{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-alpha-k-procedure-atom-knot-mass-preamble","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:alpha-k-procedure-atom-knot-mass-preamble","kind":"prose","text":"alpha-k-procedure-atom-knot-mass-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:alpha-k-procedure-atom-knot-mass-preamble\"></a><p>We now derive the atom-knot mass. We assemble the joint-tower SDP confinement constraints and identify the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">y_\\lambda</code> closed-form Wenzl bridge. This yields the per-atom-knot mass coefficient table.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/alpha-k-procedure-atom-knot-mass-intro.md","heading":""}
